9&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0050&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 72308647&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-12-22&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 145144&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 145515&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0.058611&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 27<br />00217&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0051&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 72308647&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-12-22&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 170642&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 170720&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0.010556&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 27<br />00217&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0002&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 04648240&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2017-01-10&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 094342&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 094602&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0.038889&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 32<br />00206&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0010&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 04648240&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2017-01-10&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 152749&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 153236&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0.079722&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 32<br />00206&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0011&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 04648240&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2017-01-10&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 153236&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 153421&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0.029167&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 32<br />00206&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0011&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 04648240&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2017-01-10&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 153755&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 154248&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0.081389&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0<br />00211&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0010&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 04648240&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2017-01-11&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 073208&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 073302&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0.015000&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 32<br />00210&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0036&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 04648240&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2017-01-11&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 115652&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 120935&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0.211944&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 154</p><p>Je voudrais trouver, pour chaque couple id_document+id_operation, la première occurrence, seulement s&#039;il y a plusieurs occurrences et qu&#039;un autre couple vient s&#039;intercaler entre elles.</p><p>En résultat, je devrais avoir :</p><p>id_perso&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; id_operation&#160; &#160; id_document&#160; &#160; jour&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; debut&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; fin&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; temps&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; quantite<br />00212&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0001&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 72308647&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-12-19&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 091418&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 091727&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0.052500&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 27<br />00206&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0010&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 04648240&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2017-01-10&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 152749&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 153236&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0.079722&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 32</p><p>Est-ce possible SANS passer par PL/pgSQL ? peut-être avec une fonction de fenêtrage (que j&#039;ai du mal à maîtriser).</p><p>Pouvez-vous m&#039;aiguiller, svp ?</p><p>D&#039;avance merci pour votre aide.</p>]]></content>
